// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Source File : texts/Working 	Sheet : Heldenjaeger 
//
// Script      : Xlstocontactdef.bat 
// Version     : 35 
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Contact Name : Heldenjaeger 
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 
// Name :
"P255047565" "Heldenjaeger"
// ProfessionString :
"P1161795730" "Annoying Automaton"
// DescriptionString :
"P721216801" "It's unclear why Nemesis chose to use this Jaeger automaton as a propaganda mouthpiece, rather than utilizing its combat potential. It's possible that Nemesis has begun to value psychological warfare as much as the conventional kind. Or, perhaps, this unit's weapon systems are malfunctioning, and he is simply making the best of a failed creation. However, the more that 'Heldenjaeger' (as this thing calls itself) speaks to you, the more you begin to suspect a more disturbing possibility: that this automaton <i>decided</i> to cheer on Nemesis publicly, in a show of loyalty to its master."
// LocationString :
"P3493519327" "Steel Canyon"
// InteractionRequiresText :
"P1967663612" "<color orange>In order to play Heldenjaeger's storyarc, you will need to have purchased the fifth episode of the second signature story arc, <i>Pandora's Box</i>, or be a VIP subscriber."
// TaskForceInvite :
"P2492266214" "<color orange>This Jaeger automaton appears to be moving erratically, and its speakers are blaring a brassy marching song reminiscent of Ride of the Valkyries. It doesn't seem to be taking a threatening stance, or brandishing weapons of any sort. When you approach, the music cuts off abruptly, and a tinny voice begins to emit from the Jaeger's speakers.</color><br><br>Greetings, {HeroName}! Have you come to pay homage to our great Lord Nemesis? Thanks in no small part to your efforts, his might will soon span the entire globe!<br><br>Or... perhaps you have the hubris to oppose him? A laughable notion, indeed, but not atypical of so-called 'Heroes' like yourself!"
// PlayerLevelTooLow :
"P2393762649" "<color orange>This Jaeger automaton appears to be moving erratically, and its speakers are blaring a brassy marching song reminiscent of Ride of the Valkyries. It doesn't seem to be taking a threatening stance, or brandishing weapons of any sort.<br><br>When you approach, the music modulates slightly. Instead of echoing German, the choir in the song begins to sing in heavily-accented English instead:</color><br><br>Not level 40, not level 40, too weak for our Lord to even subdue. Nemesis rising, Nemesis rising, fighting powers much greater than you!"
// PlayerLevelTooHigh :
// NeedTeamLeader :
"P1879755616" "<color orange>This Jaeger automaton appears to be moving erratically, and its speakers are blaring a brassy marching song reminiscent of Ride of the Valkyries. It doesn't seem to be taking a threatening stance, or brandishing weapons of any sort.<br><br>When you approach, the music modulates slightly. Instead of echoing German, the choir in the song begins to sing in heavily-accented English instead:</color><br><br>You follow, we lead! Your leader, we need! A peon will not do, bring the leader of your crew!"
// NeedTeamOnMap :
"P3279970138" "<color orange>This Jaeger automaton appears to be moving erratically, and its speakers are blaring a brassy marching song reminiscent of Ride of the Valkyries. It doesn't seem to be taking a threatening stance, or brandishing weapons of any sort.<br><br>When you approach, the music modulates slightly. Instead of echoing German, the choir in the song begins to sing in heavily-accented English instead:</color><br><br>You alone will have no hope, our Lord's plan is grand in scope! If it's Nemesis you fight, bring your team's entire might!"
// BadTeamLevel :
"P1240561338" "<color orange>This Jaeger automaton appears to be moving erratically, and its speakers are blaring a brassy marching song reminiscent of Ride of the Valkyries. It doesn't seem to be taking a threatening stance, or brandishing weapons of any sort.<br><br>When you approach, the music modulates slightly. Instead of echoing German, the choir in the song begins to sing in heavily-accented English instead:</color><br><br>Your strength is grand, we will confess, but your cadre is not the best. You'd best get friends, 40 all, or their weakness will be your fall!"
// TaskForceName :
"P57616970" "{HeroName}"
// HelloString :
"P2572855101" "Are you prepared to give in yet, {HeroName}?"
// HelloString :
"P910501234" "You have no chance, {HeroName}. Struggling will only make your defeat that much more painful!"
// HelloString :
"P2044425404" "Hail Lord Nemesis!"
// -------------------------------------------------------------------------------- 


